<title>EU: EP DEBATES ILLEGAL EXPORT OF BRITISH BEEF.</title>
<headline>EP DEBATES ILLEGAL EXPORT OF BRITISH BEEF.</headline>
<text>
<p>EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT SESSION NEWS PRESS RELEASE</p>
<p>DOCUMENT DATE: JULY 15, 1997</p>
<p>*</p>
<p>Illegal export of British beef</p>
<p>*</p>
<p>Tuesday, 15 July - Sirkka-Liisa Anttila (Fin, ELDR) asked what steps had been taken to establish whether the reports were correct that beef had been exported from the United Kingdom in contravention of the ban. Commissioner Emma Bonino confirmed that a case had come to light of illegal export of 1650 tonnes of British beef. The Commission, she said, had asked the British Government to withdraw approval of the offending companies. She also revealed that the Commission would be employing 35 more veterinary inspectors by the end of the year so that they could intensify the checks. She could not say that there had been no other cases of illegal exports.</p>
<p>END OF DOCUMENT</p>
